; regression test: `break` written at the very top level of a file (not inside any `sandbox`
; the file itself opened) used to crash with an internal `AssertionError` instead of a clean
; error -- a file's top level is *already* an implicit `sandbox` (see doc/kurt-doc.md's
; "Running a file itself already starts one level deep" note), so `break` there used to
; happily close that hidden wrapper instead of refusing outright, breaking `load_file`'s own
; bookkeeping (it expects to be the only one popping that particular level). Fixed via
; `KnowledgeBase.is_load_boundary`, set only on that implicit level.
;
; note: this can't use `expect` -- inside an `expect` block, `break` would close that block
; instead of reaching the top level, so the `;;; ` marker convention is used.
bool A
use A
break
;;; EvalError: `break` has no block to close here -- this is the top level of the file, not a `sandbox` you opened yourself
